# Example model: Qwen3.8-27B AWQ, as measured on 2026-11-01 (context 16384, 16 sequences, one prefill length).
# It keeps the same mounts and tuned-config folder as the 35B file, because that is how it was measured: every arm of that run
# mounted variant C and set the tuned folder. Values are data: never expanded, never executed.
MODEL_DIR=/root/.cache/huggingface/local/Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ
SERVED_NAME=qwen3.8-27b
MAX_MODEL_LEN=16384
MAX_NUM_SEQS=16
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85
PREFILL_LENS=8192
# MOE_DTYPE=int4_w4a16 (the default; the weight dtype of the MoE layers for `moe-tune`; `none` means the model has no MoE layers)
# MOE_ACT_DTYPE=bfloat16 (the default; the activation dtype `moe-tune` tunes the experts layer for). It is the default and was NOT measured for this model: whether this model serves BF16
# or FP16 was not checked. A tuning for the wrong activation dtype can be slower than the default (§ 15.3 of the 35B model's results); set float16 here if the server runs FP16.
TUNED_CONFIG_DIR=/work/moe/tune/merged
MOUNTS="C/auto_gptq.py:/opt/python/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/auto_gptq.py:ro C/gptq_utils.py:/opt/python/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/utils/gptq_utils.py:ro"
EXTRA_SERVE_ARGS="--limit-mm-per-prompt.image 0 --limit-mm-per-prompt.video 0"
# LINEAR_SHAPES= is left empty: not measured for the AWQ path (whether this model takes the hybrid W4A16 kernel is not known), so `linear-bench` refuses this file.
